A||N||1||Vlad||What kind of oil pressure unit do I want?||||5||
Z||000000||Vlad||04-28-2001||11:29 PM||||Hello all,<P>Going to replace oil pressure unit, I was asked at the shop if I wanted 60 PSI or 80 PSI unit. <BR>The biggest number on my oil pressure gauge is 550. No kidding.........  Some king of metric stuff.<P>So I don't know what kind of sender I want to buy.<P>Please, advice......||||reg||5
Z||000001||Spektyr||04-29-2001||07:32 AM||||Well, the oil pressure gauge on my V6 just so happens to have 80psi as the top mark, and I've had readings of about 60-65psi at wide open throttle, so I'm guessing you want the 80psi model.<P>I'd think my car would blow the thing right out of the block if I put a 60psi on mine.<P>I could be wrong, though.<P>According to my Haynes manual the 4 cylinder should put out 36 to 41 psi at 2,000 rpm.  For some reason it doesn't list oil pressure on the 2.8 V6.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
